A||||9||4Banger Bandit||I got an '87 GT fastback today!!!
Z||000000||4Banger Bandit||08-25-99||08:36 PM||||Whoopeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeeee, I finally got V6 power in my Fiero!  As you probably already know from my previous post, I got it from a repairables lot, but it's already looking good.  I've already got a brand new windshield in it, and removed the thrashed hood.  Tomorrow it gets it's new hood, new headlight assemblies, and a fender.  It's got power EVERYTHING, sunroof, subwoofer, spoiler and some other assorted goodies.  Anybody know the RPO codes for gear ratio's?  I'm curious what the gears are.  The previous owner had rigged up some sort of alarm sytem, and there is a red light that is constantly flashing on the console.  Also, the parking brake seems to be stuck on and I can disenguage it! Any ideas?  thanks guys..
Z||000001||Cliff Pennock||08-26-99||02:20 AM||||Congratulations!<p>About the parking brake, you'll have to replace the cable. Once the cable gets stuck, there really isn't a way to loosen it up again... If you look under your car at the rear end, you'll notice a cable running from one wheel to the other. In the middle it splits three ways, one cable going to the lever inside the car. Here you can tighten/loosen the cable. The part that needs replacement is the part that goes to the lever.
Z||000002||Formula||08-26-99||10:34 AM||||Is it man. or auto. Congrats. does it have the diamond star wheels on it?
Z||000003||four50four||08-26-99||12:15 PM||||congrats on your new car! if you don't mind me asking, how much did you end up paying for it?
Z||000004||4Banger Bandit||08-26-99||01:47 PM||||four50four, the car ended up costing me $2000, and the windshield was smashed, so it cost another 120 bucks to fix that. Everything else it needs is coming off my 4Banger Fiero, and it doesn't need much. And yeah, it's got the silver diamond spoke rims with a set of newish Pirelli rubber on them.  Didn't all GT fastbacks have the diamond spokes?? Anyhow, when I first got the car it was dying at idle, so I figured it could use a major tune-up.  So far all I've done is a K&W motor flush, oil change with filter, and a fuel filter, and it no longer dies while idling.  Also, the thermostat pressure cap was leaking coolant bad, so I had that replaced and it's all hunky dorey now. The car still seems to have a little bit of a miss, but I think the plugs and wires will cure that.  It's still got the origional AC Delco wires with the funky ends on them.   OH, and thanks for the advice on the E-Brake cable Cliff! 
Z||000005||four50four||08-26-99||02:32 PM||||i still think you got a great deal. i wish i could find a gt for that price! <IMG SRC="/ubb/smile.gif" WIDTH=15 HEIGHT=15>
